                {%- comment -%}
                  A "clean" logo URL that more than one store resolves to is
                  ignored — see ss-one-lookup, which collects them in the same
                  single pass that reads everything else.

                  The dashboard prefers logo_clean_url (a background-removed
                  copy) over the store's own logo media. When that field is
                  stale or was written wrong, a run of stores all render the
                  same picture: four in a row showed one logo on the dashboard
                  while each store page, which reads entry.logo, showed the
                  correct one. A clean URL shared by two stores is not a
                  store's logo by definition, so those fall back to the logo
                  media and nothing has to be migrated.
                {%- endcomment -%}

                {%- comment -%}
                  Counted here rather than taken from forloop.index0, because
                  sorted_blob is "||a||||b||" and splitting it yields empty
                  segments the loop skips. Using the loop index would push real
                  stores past the first page and show fewer than ten.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign ss_rendered = 0 -%}
                {% for rec in store_records %}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Everything this card needs was read once, at the top:
                      see ss-one-lookup. Fields, in order — handle, ready,
                      collection handle, product count, status, clean logo url,
                      logo url, large logo url, name, and a constant terminator
                      so a blank name is never the last field.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {% assign f = rec | split: ss_fs %}
                    {% assign handle = f[0] | default: '' | strip %}
                    {% if handle != blank %}

                    {% assign is_fully_ready = false %}
                    {% if f[1] == '1' %}{% assign is_fully_ready = true %}{% endif %}

                    {% assign collection_handle = f[2] %}
                    {% if collection_handle == blank %}{% assign collection_handle = handle %}{% endif %}

                    {% assign product_count = f[3] | plus: 0 %}
                    {% assign tile_status = f[4] | default: '' %}

                    {%- comment -%}
                      A clean URL two stores share is not either store's logo,
                      so it is dropped and the logo media takes over.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {% assign tile_logo_clean = blank %}
                    {% assign lcu = f[5] | default: '' %}
                    {% if lcu != blank %}
                      {% assign clean_uses = all_clean_urls | split: lcu | size | minus: 1 %}
                      {% if clean_uses <= 1 %}{% assign tile_logo_clean = lcu %}{% endif %}
                    {% endif %}

                    {%- comment -%}
                      The logo media wins over the background-removed copy.
                      The store page renders entry.logo and has always shown
                      the right mark; the dashboard preferred the clean copy,
                      which is a second field that can drift out of sync with
                      the first and did. One source for both surfaces means a
                      correct store page can no longer sit beside a wrong card.
                      The clean copy stays as the fallback for stores that only
                      ever had one.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {% assign tile_logo_file = f[6] | default: '' %}
                    {% assign tile_onboarding_image = blank %}
                    {% if tile_logo_file != blank %}
                      {% assign tile_logo_clean = blank %}
                      {% assign tile_onboarding_image = f[7] | default: '' %}
                    {% elsif tile_logo_clean != blank %}
                      {% assign tile_onboarding_image = tile_logo_clean %}
                    {% endif %}

                    {% assign tile_name = f[8] | default: '' %}
                    {% if tile_name == blank %}{% assign tile_name = handle | replace: '-', ' ' | capitalize %}{% endif %}

                    {% assign tile_url = routes.collections_url | append: '/' | append: collection_handle %}
                    {% capture admin_url %}/pages/admin-powers?shop={{ handle | url_encode }}{% endcapture %}

                    {% capture admin_needle2 %}||{{ handle }}||{% endcapture %}
                    {% assign tile_is_admin = false %}
                    {% if admin_handles_blob contains admin_needle2 %}{% assign tile_is_admin = true %}{% endif %}

                    {%- comment %} Sleep/waking status, from the record. {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- assign tile_is_sleeping = false -%}
                    {%- assign tile_is_waking = false -%}
                    {%- if tile_status == 'sleeping' -%}{%- assign tile_is_sleeping = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- if tile_status == 'waking' -%}{%- assign tile_is_waking = true -%}{%- endif -%}

                    {%- comment -%}
                      ss-paged-card marks a card the pager and the search box
                      own. The tool cards above (Command Center, Price Editor
                      and friends) deliberately carry neither: they are not
                      stores, so they should not be hidden behind "show more"
                      or vanish when someone searches for a team name.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- assign tile_position = ss_rendered -%}
                    {%- assign ss_rendered = ss_rendered | plus: 1 -%}
                    <div
                      class="ss-store-card ss-paged-card{% if is_fully_ready and tile_is_sleeping == false and tile_is_waking == false %} ss-clickrow{% endif %}{% if ss_paging_on and tile_position >= ss_page_size %} ss-card-paged-out{% endif %}"
                      role="link"
                      tabindex="0"
                      data-href="{{ tile_url }}"
                      data-ss-handle="{{ handle | escape }}"
                      data-ss-name="{{ tile_name | escape }}"
                      data-ss-position="{{ tile_position }}"
                      data-ss-backend="{{ section.settings.backend_url | escape }}"
                      data-ss-products="{{ product_count }}"
                      data-ss-ready="{% if is_fully_ready and tile_is_sleeping == false and tile_is_waking == false %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
                      data-ss-building="{% if tile_is_waking %}1{% elsif tile_is_sleeping == false and is_fully_ready == false %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
                      data-ss-onboarding-admin="{% if tile_is_admin or is_god %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
                      data-ss-onboarding-image="{{ tile_onboarding_image | escape }}"
                      data-admin-href="{{ admin_url }}"
                      data-ss-bootstrapper="{% if tile_is_admin or is_god %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
                      data-ss-sleep-status="{% if tile_is_sleeping %}sleeping{% elsif tile_is_waking %}waking{% else %}active{% endif %}"
                      style="{% if tile_is_sleeping %} opacity:0.65; border-color:rgba(99,102,241,0.4);{% elsif tile_is_waking %} border-color:rgba(59,130,246,0.5);{% endif %}"
                    >

                      <div class="ss-col-identity">
                        {%- comment -%}
                          The resolved source is stamped on the frame so this
                          is checkable from the page itself. Three rounds were
                          spent arguing about whether a wrong logo came from
                          the server or from JavaScript; one attribute settles
                          it, and it costs nothing.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        {%- comment -%}
                          Cards past the first page start hidden, so their
                          logos are lazy: an account with sixty stores was
                          opening sixty image connections before the first ten
                          cards had painted. The visible page stays eager, so
                          nothing about WHEN a shown logo resolves has changed.

                          This does not reopen the wrong-logo bug the notes
                          below describe. That one was srcset and JS rewriting
                          choosing a different picture than the src; there is
                          still no srcset here and still nothing rewriting it.
                          Deferring a hidden image changes when it loads, not
                          which one it is.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        {%- if ss_paging_on and tile_position >= ss_page_size -%}{%- assign tile_loading = 'lazy' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign tile_loading = 'eager' -%}{%- endif -%}
                        {%- comment -%}
                          Why a card has no logo, stamped where it can be read
                          off the page: 'shared' means a clean URL was found
                          but another store had the same one, so it was dropped
                          as not being either store's; 'missing' means the
                          metaobject offered nothing at all. Three rounds were
                          spent arguing about where a wrong logo came from; one
                          attribute settles it, and it costs nothing.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        {%- assign tile_resolved = f[9] | default: '0' -%}
                        {%- assign tile_logo_why = 'clean' -%}
                        {%- if tile_logo_file != blank -%}{%- assign tile_logo_why = 'file' -%}
                        {%- elsif tile_logo_clean == blank -%}
                          {%- if lcu != blank -%}{%- assign tile_logo_why = 'shared' -%}
                          {%- else -%}{%- assign tile_logo_why = 'missing' -%}{%- endif -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        <div class="ss-logo-frame"
                             data-ss-logo-for="{{ handle | escape }}"
                             data-ss-logo-why="{{ tile_logo_why }}"
                             data-ss-entry="{{ tile_resolved }}"
                             data-ss-logo-kind="{% if tile_logo_clean != blank %}clean{% elsif tile_logo_file != blank %}file{% else %}none{% endif %}">
                          {% if tile_logo_clean != blank %}
                            <img
                              src="{{ tile_logo_clean | escape }}"
                              loading="{{ tile_loading }}"
                              decoding="async"
                              alt="{{ tile_name | escape }}"
                              width="72"
                              height="72">
                          {% elsif tile_logo_file != blank %}
                            {%- comment -%}
                              Sized here, in Liquid, rather than upgraded by JS
                              after load. A script that rewrites src/srcset is
                              a script that can put one store's picture on
                              another's card, which is exactly what happened —
                              and it re-ran on every DOM mutation, which is
                              what made a long dashboard stutter while
                              scrolling. Shopify builds the correct srcset from
                              the file itself, so nothing has to run at all.
                            {%- endcomment -%}
                            {%- comment -%}
                              One src, no srcset, and no lazy loading.

                              A browser renders whichever candidate srcset
                              selects and ignores src entirely, so a srcset is
                              the only attribute that can make an <img> display
                              a picture other than the one in its src. At
                              72-92px it buys nothing worth that risk.

                              Lazy loading is gone for the same reason: it is
                              the one behaviour here that makes WHEN an image
                              resolves depend on scroll position, and every
                              version of this bug has been a run of trailing
                              cards — the ones furthest down — wearing one
                              store's logo. A dashboard shows a handful of
                              stores for almost everyone, and these are ~10KB
                              logos at 92px, so deferring them was saving
                              nothing measurable while making the load order
                              unpredictable.

                              Width 512 covers the largest frame (92px) at 3x
                              device pixel ratio with room to spare, since
                              there is no srcset to pick a sharper candidate.
                            {%- endcomment -%}
                            {%- comment -%}
                              Written out rather than run through image_tag,
                              because the record carries a URL and image_tag
                              needs the media object. image_tag was only ever
                              being asked for one src with no srcset, so the
                              markup below is what it emitted anyway.
                            {%- endcomment -%}
                            <img
                              src="{{ tile_logo_file | escape }}"
                              loading="{{ tile_loading }}"
                              decoding="async"
                              alt="{{ tile_name | escape }}"
                              width="72"
                              height="72">
                          {% else %}
                            <span class="ss-logo-fallback">{{ tile_name | slice: 0, 2 | upcase }}</span>
                          {% endif %}
                        </div>

                        <div class="ss-identity-text">
                          <h3 class="ss-card-title">{{ tile_name }}</h3>
                          <span class="ss-card-subtitle">Private Collection</span>
                        </div>
                      </div>

                      <div class="ss-col-engine">
                        {% if is_fully_ready and tile_is_sleeping == false and tile_is_waking == false %}
                          <div class="ss-status-finished">
                            <span class="ss-dot-live"></span>
                            <span class="ss-status-text">LIVE STOREFRONT</span>
                          </div>
                        {% elsif tile_is_sleeping %}
                          <div class="ss-status-finished ss-status-hibernating">
                            <span class="ss-dot-live ss-dot-hibernating"></span>
                            <span class="ss-status-text">HIBERNATING STORE</span>
                          </div>
                        {% elsif tile_is_waking or is_fully_ready == false %}
