    {%- comment -%}
      STELLA & SAGE ANTI-FLASH GUARD

      Thirty-two of this theme's sections emit their markup BEFORE their own
      <style> block — seller-dashboard puts 82KB of HTML ahead of its CSS,
      landing-dual-hub 18KB. A browser paints what it has, so those pages show
      raw unstyled markup for a moment and then snap into place. It does not
      read as loading; it reads as a broken site.

      So the page is held at opacity 0 until its styles are in, and revealed
      once. Every page, with no list of routes.

      There WAS a list here, naming collections, products and eight or so
      /pages/ paths. The home page was not on it, and neither was anything
      added since — which is why this came back looking worse than before. The
      list was also duplicated between the two scripts below, so covering a new
      page meant remembering both. Guarding everything costs a few frames on
      pages that never flashed and cannot silently miss one that does.

      Two independent safety nets, because a page stuck at opacity 0 is far
      worse than a flash:
        - the hard timeout below reveals the page even if the release script
          never runs, and it is registered in the SAME block that hides it, so
          no failure can hide without also scheduling the reveal;
        - with JavaScript off, nothing adds the class in the first place, and
          the noscript rule makes that explicit rather than incidental.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function () {
        document.documentElement.className += ' ss-internal-booting ss-route-booting';
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className
            .replace(/\bss-internal-booting\b/g, '')
            .replace(/\bss-route-booting\b/g, '');
          if (document.documentElement.className.indexOf('ss-internal-ready') === -1) {
